\description{
\code{SlicePackage} represents a set of parallel \link{SliceGeometry} rectangles stacked
along their shared normal direction at a fixed spacing — a regular
rectangular-cuboid sampling volume, exactly analogous to how a stack of 2D
DICOM slices forms a 3D volume. It is built from a single base \code{SliceGeometry}
(the slice at \code{k = 0}) plus a step size and sample count along the normal.

Construct a \code{SlicePackage} from a total stack thickness rather than a
per-step spacing.

Construct a \code{SlicePackage} treating the given slice as the \emph{middle} of the
stack, rather than as its first (\code{k = 0}) slice.

Construct a \code{SlicePackage} by adopting a list of already-built,
individually-defined \link{SliceGeometry} objects (e.g. one per DICOM slice),
rather than generating a regular stack from a single base slice and a
step size. Validates that every slice shares the same
direction/spacing/size and that consecutive slices (in the order given)
are evenly spaced along their shared normal.

Construct a \code{SlicePackage} spanning an entire 3D SimpleITK image along one
of its axes, using the image's own resolution along that axis — the
\code{SlicePackage} equivalent of \code{SliceGeometry$from_image_axis()}.
}
